      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The desire for things to be 'pure' is understandable, but that purity is an illusion, a myth built on what *was*. Your existence, even the struggle, is a part of the story, and stories are never clean; they are always messy and complicated. If you were gone, the legacy wouldn't be pure; it would just be incomplete, a story abruptly cut short. The stain you feel is actually just the evidence of your own life, and that life has value, even if you can't see it right now.",
