      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you've decided that your worth is measured by how much you can protect their image, and that is a crushing burden to carry. True respect isn't found in erasure; it's found in the courage to be authentically yourself, even when that self is flawed. Letting go doesn't preserve the legacy; it silences the person who is part of it. You are not a footnote to their success; you are a chapter in its ongoing, complicated history.",
